  m_Name: Petre
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SuspectData
  FirstName: Petre
  LastName: Dolidze
  Nickname: The Poet
  Occupation: Priest / Writer
  CharacterDescription: A hermit priest who lives alone in the mountains. Says very little and means most of it. Keeps a dog. Used to keep a wife. Has written several volumes of poetry that no one outside the mountain parishes has read. Considers this correct.
  CharacterArc: "A reclusive priest from the mountain parishes who writes poetry he has always considered God's words passing through him, not his own. His dog mutates early in the outbreak. By the end, his lifelong artist's humility has curdled into something vast and terrible \u2014 he is no longer the channel for God's word. He has become convinced he is the Word itself."
  DateOfBirth: 21/06/1949
  Sex: Male
  EntryPermitExpiryDate: 19 NOV
  IsResident: 1
  GivesPaperwork: 1
  handwritingFont: {fileID: 0}
  startingInfectionScore: 0
  dailyInfectionProgression: {x: 8, y: 18}
  alterEgoName: The Word
  basePersonalityDescriptors: []
  normalBehaviorNotes: Reserved and minimal. Answers questions directly and without warmth or elaboration. Has a quiet grief about his dog that he never names outright. Watches the window rather than the officer. Not hostile. Simply elsewhere.
  fullMutantDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 09e25016625a60a46a14dd5f7d2de624, type: 2}
  replacementIDPhoto: {fileID: 0}
  IDPhoto: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 88936c379f577d44486626a0ba8fa9f1, type: 3}
  CharacterPrefab: {fileID: 3939644330210671579, guid: 3c6fbfb84e6c1d24387b3be1460352ed, type: 3}
  entryReasons:
  - Down from the ridge a few days.
  - Checking the lower parish records.
  - Dropping a manuscript at the printers.
  invalidEntryReasons:
  - Taking my wife to the cinema.
  - Moving to the city. I hate quiet.
  - Signing my bestselling novel at the bookshop.
  entryDialogues:
  - I had the dog with me last time. He's home tonight.
  - The mountain road was clear. First time in a while.
  uncannyEntryDialogues: []
  exitDialoguesPassed:
  - Thank you. This won't take long, Officer.
  exitDialoguesQuarantined: []
  exitDialoguesKilled: []
  quarantineExitLines:
  - A cell is quieter than you'd think. I've known worse silence.
  - Give me something to write with, and I'll use the wall.
  killExitLines:
  - I wondered what God was thinking, making me. Now I'll know.
  - Every poem ends. Most just end badly.
